\mt1 2 Peter
\c 1
\s1 A Greeting from Peter
\r (\ref 1 Peter 1:1–2|1PE 1:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 1 Simon Peter, a servant and apostle of Jesus Christ,
\p To those who through \add the\add* righteousness of our God and Savior Jesus Christ have received a faith as precious as ours:
\p \v 2 Grace and peace be multiplied to you through \add the\add* knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord.
\s1 Partakers of the Divine Nature
\p \v 3 His divine power has given us everything \add we need\add* for life and godliness through the knowledge of Him who called us \add by His\add* own\f + \fr 1:3 \ft Or \fqa to His own\f* glory and excellence. \v 4 Through \add these\add* He has given us \add His\add* precious and magnificent promises, so that through \add them\add* you may become partakers of \add the\add* divine nature, now that you have escaped the corruption in the world caused by evil desires.
\p \v 5 For this very \add reason\add*, make every effort to add to your faith virtue; and to virtue, knowledge; \v 6 and to knowledge, self-control; and to self-control, perseverance; and to perseverance, godliness; \v 7 and to godliness, brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness, love. \v 8 For \add if\add* you possess these \add qualities \add* and continue to grow \add in them\add*, they will keep you from being ineffective and unproductive in \add your\add* knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ. \v 9 \add But\add* whoever lacks these \add traits \add* is nearsighted to the point of blindness, having forgotten that he has been cleansed from his past sins.
\p \v 10 Therefore, brothers, strive to make your calling and election sure. For if you practice these things \add you will\add* never stumble, \v 11 and you will receive a lavish reception into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.
\p \v 12 Therefore I will always remind you of these things, even though you know \add them\add* and are established in the truth you now have. \v 13 I think it is right to refresh your memory as long as I \add live\add* in the tent \add of my body \add*,\f + \fr 1:13 \ft Literally \fqa as long as I am in this tent\f* \v 14 because I know that this tent will soon be laid aside, as our Lord Jesus Christ has made clear to me. \v 15 And I will make every effort to ensure \add that\add* after my departure, you will be able to recall these things at all times.
\s1 Eyewitnesses of His Majesty
\r (\ref Matthew 17:1–13|MAT 17:1-13\ref*; \ref Mark 9:1–13|MRK 9:1-13\ref*; \ref Luke 9:28–36|LUK 9:28-36\ref*)
\p \v 16 For we did not follow cleverly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of His majesty. \v 17 For He received honor and glory from God \add the\add* Father \add when\add* the voice came to Him from the Majestic Glory, saying, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.”\f + \fr 1:17 \ref Matthew 17:5|MAT 17:5\ref*; see also Mark 9:7 and Luke 9:35.\f* \v 18 And we ourselves heard this voice from heaven \add when\add* we were with Him on the holy mountain.
\p \v 19 We also have the word of the prophets as confirmed beyond doubt. \add And\add* you will do well to pay attention to it, as to a lamp shining in \add a\add* dark place, until \add the\add* day dawns and \add the\add* morning star rises in your hearts. \v 20 Above all, you must understand that no prophecy of Scripture comes from \add one’s\add* own interpretation. \v 21 For no \add such\add* prophecy \add was\add* ever brought forth by \add the\add* will of man, but men spoke from God as they were carried along by \add the\add* Holy Spirit.
\c 2
\s1 Deliverance from False Prophets
\r (\ref Jude 1:3–16|JUD 3-16\ref*)
\p \v 1 Now there were also false prophets among the people, just as there will be false teachers among you. \add They\add* will secretly introduce destructive heresies, even denying the Master who bought them — bringing swift destruction on themselves. \v 2 Many will follow in their depravity, \add and\add* because of \add them\add* the way of truth will be defamed. \v 3 In their greed, \add these false teachers\add* will exploit you with deceptive words. The longstanding verdict against them remains in force, and their destruction \add does\add* not sleep.
\p \v 4 For if God \add did\add* not spare \add the\add* angels when they sinned, but cast \add them\add* deep into hell,\f + \fr 2:4 \ft Greek \fqa cast them into Tartarus\ft ; see the First Book of Enoch (1 Enoch 13:1–11 and 1 Enoch 20:1–4).\f* placing \add them\add* in chains of darkness to be held for judgment; \v 5 \add if\add* He did not spare \add the\add* ancient world when He brought \add the\add* flood \add on its\add* ungodly \add people\add*, but preserved Noah, a preacher of righteousness, among the eight; \v 6 \add if\add* He condemned \add the\add* cities of Sodom and Gomorrah to destruction,\f + \fr 2:6 \ft WH does not include \fqa to destruction\ft .\f* reducing \add them\add* to ashes \add as\add* an example of what is coming on the ungodly;\f + \fr 2:6 \ft Or \fqa on future generations of the ungodly\f* \v 7 and \add if\add* He rescued Lot, a righteous \add man\add* distressed by the depraved conduct of the lawless \v 8 (for that righteous \add man\add*, living among them day after day, was tormented \add in his\add* righteous soul \add by the\add* lawless deeds he saw and heard)— \v 9  \add if all this is so, then the \add* Lord knows how to rescue \add the\add* godly from trials and to hold \add the\add* unrighteous for punishment on \add the\add* day of judgment.
\p \v 10  \add Such punishment is \add* specially \add reserved\add* for those who indulge \add the\add* corrupt desires of \add the\add* flesh and despise authority. Bold \add and\add* self-willed, they are unafraid to slander glorious beings.\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Or \fqa to blaspheme angelic majesties\f* \v 11 Yet not even angels, \add though\add* greater in strength and power, dare to bring such slanderous charges against them before \add the\add* Lord.
\p \v 12 These \add men are\add* like irrational animals, creatures of instinct, born to be captured and destroyed. They blaspheme in \add matters\add* they do not understand, \add and like such creatures\add*, they too will be destroyed. \v 13 The harm they will suffer \add is the\add* wages of \add their\add* wickedness.
\p They consider it a pleasure to carouse in broad daylight. \add They are\add* blots and blemishes, reveling in their deception as they feast with you. \v 14 \add Their\add* eyes are full of adultery; their desire for sin is never satisfied; they seduce \add the\add* unstable. \add They are\add* accursed children with hearts trained in greed.
\p \v 15 They have left \add the\add* straight way and wandered off to follow the way of Balaam \add son\add* of Beor,\f + \fr 2:15 \ft NA, SBL, BYZ, and TR \fqa Bosor\f* who loved \add the\add* wages of wickedness. \v 16 But he was rebuked for his transgression by a donkey,  \add otherwise \add* without speech, that spoke with a man’s voice \add and\add* restrained the prophet’s madness.
\p \v 17 These \add men\add* are springs without water and mists driven by a storm. Blackest darkness is reserved for them. \v 18 With lofty \add but\add* empty words, they appeal \add to the\add* sensual passions of \add the\add* flesh \add and\add* entice those \add who are\add* just escaping from \add others\add* who live in error. \v 19 They promise them freedom, while they themselves are slaves to depravity. For a man is a slave to whatever has mastered him.
\p \v 20 If indeed they have escaped the corruption of the world through \add the\add* knowledge of \add our\add* Lord and Savior Jesus Christ,\f + \fr 2:20 \ft SBL and WH \fqa the Lord and Savior Jesus Christ\f* only to be entangled \add and\add* overcome by it again, their final \add condition\add* is worse than \add it was\add* at first. \v 21 It would have been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness than to have known \add it\add* and then to turn away from the holy commandment passed on to them. \v 22 Of them the proverbs are true: “A dog returns to \add its\add* vomit,”\f + \fr 2:22 \ref Proverbs 26:11|PRO 26:11\ref*\f* and, “A sow that is washed \add goes back\add* to \add her\add* wallowing in \add the\add* mud.”
\c 3
\s1 The Coming Judgment
\r (\ref Genesis 7:1–24|GEN 7:1-24\ref*; \ref Jude 1:17–23|JUD 17-23\ref*)
\p \v 1 Beloved, this \add is\add* now \add my\add* second letter to you. \add Both\add* of \add them are\add* reminders to stir you to wholesome thinking \v 2 by recalling what was foretold by the holy prophets and commanded by \add our\add* Lord and Savior through your apostles.
\p \v 3 Most importantly, you must understand that in the last days scoffers will come, scoffing \add and\add* following their own evil desires.\f + \fr 3:3 \ft See \ref Jude 1:18|JUD 18\ref*.\f* \v 4 “Where is the promise of His coming?” they will ask. “Ever since \add our\add* fathers fell asleep, everything continues as it has from \add the\add* beginning of creation.”
\p \v 5 \add But\add* they deliberately overlook the fact that long ago by God’s word \add the\add* heavens existed and \add the\add* earth was formed out of water and by water, \v 6 through which\f + \fr 3:6 \ft NA \fqa through whom\f* the world of that time perished in the flood. \v 7 And by that same word, the present heavens and earth are reserved for fire, being kept for \add the\add* day of judgment and destruction of ungodly men.
\s1 The Day of the Lord
\r (\ref Zephaniah 1:7–18|ZEP 1:7-18\ref*; \ref Malachi 4:1–6|MAL 4:1-6\ref*; \ref 1 Thessalonians 5:1–11|1TH 5:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 8 Beloved, \add do\add* not \add let this\add* one thing escape your notice: With \add the\add* Lord a day \add is\add* like a thousand years, and a thousand years \add are\add* like a day.\f + \fr 3:8 \ft See \ref Psalm 90:4|PSA 90:4\ref*.\f* \v 9 The Lord is not slow \add in keeping His\add* promise as some understand slowness, but is patient with you, not wanting anyone to perish but everyone to come to repentance.
\p \v 10 But \add the\add* Day of \add the\add* Lord will come like a thief. The heavens will disappear with a roar, \add the\add* elements will be destroyed\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Or \fqa dissolved\ft ; also in verses 11 and 12.\f* by fire, and \add the\add* earth and \add its\add* works will be laid bare.\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Or \fqa will not be found\ft . BYZ and TR \fqa will be burned up\ft ; SBL, NE, and WH \fqa will be found\ft , i.e., \fqa will be unable to hide\ft .\f*
\p \v 11 \add Since\add* everything will be destroyed in this way, what kind of \add people\add* ought you to be? You ought to conduct yourselves in holiness and godliness \v 12 as you anticipate and hasten the coming of the day of God, when \add the\add* heavens will be destroyed by fire and \add the\add* elements will melt in the heat. \v 13 But in keeping with \add God’s\add* promise, we are looking forward to a new heaven and a new earth, where righteousness dwells.
\s1 Final Exhortations
\p \v 14 Therefore, beloved, as you anticipate these things, make every effort to be found at peace— spotless and blameless in His \add sight\add*.\f + \fr 3:14 \ft Or \fqa to be found by Him in peace, without spot and without blemish.\f*
\p \v 15 Consider also that our Lord’s patience \add brings\add* salvation, just as our beloved brother Paul also wrote you with the wisdom \add God\add* gave him. \v 16  \add He writes \add* this way in all \add his\add* letters,\f + \fr 3:16 \ft Or \fqa in all the letters\f* speaking in them about \add such matters\add*. Some \add parts\add* of \add his letters\add* are hard to understand, which ignorant and unstable \add people\add* distort,\f + \fr 3:16 \ft NA \fqa will distort\f* as \add they do\add* the rest of \add the\add* Scriptures, to their own destruction.
\p \v 17 Therefore, beloved, \add since\add* you already know \add these things\add*, be on your guard so that you will not be carried away by the error of the lawless \add and\add* fall from \add your\add* secure standing. \v 18 But grow in \add the\add* grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. To Him \add be\add* the glory both now and to \add the\add* day of eternity.
\p Amen.\f + \fr 3:18 \ft NE, WH, and NA do not include \fqa Amen.\f*
